Jim King - August 1990How to setup Chemtab to work at your site..WARNING: Chemtab has only been tested under Ultrix 3.1 on a VAX 11/780.	 Chemtab will probably only work for BSD equivalent systems..	 Please send any fixes to me.. anyone who would spend time learning	  the internals and adding a few '#ifdef SYSV' would hold my utmost	  appreciation! (pulsar@lsrhs!xait.Xerox.COM)(1) Change the Makefile to suit your site.  Currently, the makefile will    compile with gcc, with the -g option for debugging.(2) Change tune.h (only what needs to be changed, for now.. pathnames etc..)(3) Change the directions on how to get to you printer at the end of cleanup.c(4) makeThat SHOULD be the extent of it.. but don't quote me on that.  I am theauthor, and I am not held responsible for any damage the program might cause,however it's not programmed to do any damage whatsoever.Read the manual pages in the directory Mans before you do anything else,please.  I realize that the directions are sketchy, but I am a programmer,not a documenter (or a commenter for that matter).. thanks! - JimYou can read Manual.User for a step-by-step instruction on version 1.2.